<section aria-labelledby="<%= guideline_anchor(:versions) %>">
  <h2 id="<%= guideline_anchor(:versions) %>">4. Versions</h2>
  <p>
    <b>A version with different specifications is a new product, not a version.</b>
    Versions are small changes or special editions that are sold with the same product name:
    a finish, a limited edition, a model number for one region. A product that measures
    differently is a separate product, because versions always show the specifications of their
    product. When something is called "Mk II" or has a different impedance, for example, it is a different product, not a different version. See <a href="#<%= guideline_anchor(:product_or_version) %>">3.1</a>.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Give the version a short name that tells what is special, for example <i>LTD 2024</i> or <i>Update 2024</i>.</li>
    <li>In the description, write what is different from the product, for example <i>"Available for a limited time in special colours."</i></li>
    <li>For dates and price, the same rules apply as for products (<a href="#<%= guideline_anchor(:dates) %>">3.6</a>, <a href="#<%= guideline_anchor(:price) %>">3.7</a>).</li>
    <li>
      If you see a version that has different specifications from its product, do not change the
      specifications of the product. Send an email to
      <%= contact_email_link %>
      so that it can be moved to a separate product.
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
